Debug mode highlights a multi-line macro call's path and `!`, as it highlights `macro_rules!` up to its name; the arguments and the one-line `include!` stay unhighlighted.
== args
--debug
input/macros.rs
== file input/macros.rs
thread_local! {
    static COUNTER: Cell<u32> = Cell::new(0);
}

include!("generated.rs");

std::impl_ops!(
    Meters
);
